    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (integer 0\u20139, read-only) right after `customerCode`. The DTO is generated from this spec at build time, so this creates the `checkDigit` field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` entry wiring `checkDigit` to a new `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits of `owner.getCustomerCode()` (doubling from the rightmost digit, subtracting 9 when >9, then `(10 - sum%10) % 10`), matching the reference algorithm in the acceptance test exactly. It returns `null` when the customer code is unassigned, consistent with the sibling `membershipNumber` mapper.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit, passes \u2014 full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
